  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "On November 26, 2026, weather authorities issued alerts for significant storm activity affecting the coast of the Southeast region of Brazil. The instability is attributed to the movement of a strong cold front across the area. Reports specifically highlight risks of precipitation exceeding 100 mm in parts of the Sao Paulo littoral. This event follows broader atmospheric warnings that had previously covered significant portions of the state of Sao Paulo earlier in the week. Meteorologists anticipate that the passing front will maintain overcast skies and hazardous weather conditions throughout the day. Residents and local authorities in the affected coastal zones remain on notice as the system advances, with the heavy rainfall posing potential challenges for regional infrastructure and public safety.",
